=> episode COUNT grows linearly in N (P ~ N/3), so no bound P <= const(c,m_0)
   can exist -- Prop. 13.2.  Every prefix is realized by a genuine positive odd
   integer, whose bit length grows like S_N ~ 1.4 N: the realizer height is the
   price, and it is exactly what Remark 13.3's charge re-levies at each episode.
